    description: "WI-ripas shipped the python DDG key fix (methods 0 -> 21,275 of 24,941 matched,\n§3a walks 84 -> 122) WITHOUT satisfying the A/B it demanded. This row carries\nthat debt, with the refutation pre-registered so it cannot be retro-fitted to\nwhatever the number turns out to be.\n\nPRE-REGISTERED REFUTATION, written 2026-09-22 BEFORE any precision number\nexists: if ADR-0046 USEFUL PRECISION (the second number -- correctness\nexcluding the structurally-identified class) DROPS after WI-ripas relative to\nthe same frame before it, then the fix is a REPORTING regression even though\nthe lookup it repaired was unambiguously correct, and the right response is to\nreconsider how a walk-that-escaped is labelled -- NOT to revert the key fix,\nwhich restores information that was being discarded.\n\nWHY THE RISK IS REAL AND NOT HYPOTHETICAL. Of the +38 walks WI-ripas made\npossible on this repository, +32 returned None (the walk ran and ESCAPED) and\nonly +6 established dependence. A finding that was `structural` sat OUTSIDE the\nuseful-precision denominator by ADR-0046's construction; once the walk is\nreachable it leaves that class and enters the denominator. If those escapes are\nmostly wrong, the published headline (24.1% -> 30.9% across measurements\n0003-0012) moves down for a change that improved the underlying analysis.\n\nWHY IT COULD NOT BE MEASURED IN THE SHIPPING SESSION -- three independent dead\nends, recorded so they are not re-walked:\n  1. hypergumbo's OWN claims: all 18 verdicts are `inconclusive` with zero\n     evidence. Both previously-violated self-claims were repaired, and\n     verify_claims never downgrades a `violated` verdict, so the population is\n     empty BY CONSTRUCTION. This is the same frame collapse measure-taint-\n     precision.py's docstring already records for WI-sivuz.\n  2. prospector under docs/example-claims/generic-taint-claims.yaml: 7\n     verdicts, all inconclusive, zero evidence, on both the default and the\n     --include-non-production-sources arm.\n  3. scripts/measure-taint-precision.py is a collect/sample/score/packet\n     instrument requiring PER-FLOW HUMAN SCORING against a rubric. It cannot be\n     run end-to-end by an agent in one session, by design.\n\nSO THE FIRST DELIVERABLE IS A POPULATION, NOT A NUMBER: a repo + claims pair\nthat actually produces violating python flows rooted in METHODS. Until that\nexists, no arm of this question is answerable, and finding one is the work.\n\nWHAT THE FINER INSTRUMENT BUYS. INV-zidur (satisfied) added\nTaintFlowFinding.walk_verdict and derives analysis_method from it, so\n\"walk escaped\" and \"walk proved no dependence\" are now distinguishable where\nthey were not when ddg_mixed was last measured BELOW structural. Any re-run\nshould report the walk_verdict distribution, not just analysis_method -- the\nthree-populations result that made this row refuse to ship blind was measured\nunder the COARSER vocabulary and may not survive the finer one.\n\nMEASUREMENTS TO PRODUCE, same frame both arms, ADR-0048 frame declaration\nrequired: analysis_method distribution, walk_verdict distribution, correctness,\nuseful precision -- at the commit before cadcfc8202 and at/after it."  # 2f68
    fields: {}  # 2f68
- op: discuss  # df75
  at: '2026-09-22T08:39:01Z'  # df75
  by: agent  # df75
  actor: jgstern_agent  # df75
  clock: 2  # df75
  nonce: df75  # df75
  message: "BOTH DELIVERABLES DONE, AND THE REFUTATION TURNED OUT TO BE NOT APPLICABLE\nbecause I had misread ADR-0046 when I pre-registered it. Correcting that first,\nbecause it is the load-bearing part.\n\nTHE CORRECTION. I wrote the refutation as \"if ADR-0046 useful precision DROPS\n... it should not ship as-is\", on the reasoning that a finding leaving the\nstructurally-identified class ENTERS the useful-precision denominator. Read\nagainst ADR-0046 itself, that is wrong twice:\n\n  useful precision = (TP - VACUOUS) / adjudicated, over the SAME DENOMINATOR --\n  \"the deduction is from the numerator only, so the two figures are directly\n  comparable and useful <= correctness always.\"\n\n  VACUOUS has exactly two member classes: CONFIGURED-ACTION (three citable\n  clauses -- declared-configuration source, schema deserialization,\n  field-parameterized sink) and KIND-MISDECLARED (the INV-nular defect).\n\nNEITHER keys on analysis_method. Nothing moves into or out of that denominator\nby changing an evidence label. The word \"structural\" means two unrelated things\nin the two places, and I carried my own LIVE.md shorthand into a claim about a\ndocument without reading the document -- exactly what rule 1 says not to do.\nSo the refutation is NOT APPLICABLE, not \"untested\". The risk recorded on\nWI-ripas, in its commit message and in the changelog was not real; the changelog\nis corrected on dev.\n\nDELIVERABLE 1 -- A POPULATION, which this row said had to come before any\nnumber. FOUND, and recorded so it is not re-derived:\n  ~/whole_bunch_of_repos/podman-compose  + docs/example-claims/generic-taint-claims.yaml\n  ~/whole_bunch_of_repos/sherpa-onnx     + the same claims file\nBoth yield violated verdicts WITH evidence. Dead ends confirmed and recorded:\nhypergumbo's own claims (all repaired -> zero violating flows by construction),\nprospector (7 verdicts, zero evidence, both arms), emscripten (did not complete\nwithin 580s).\n\nDELIVERABLE 2 -- THE A/B. Same binary except the two python spec hooks; the\nbefore-arm is the shipped tree with name_for/kind_for removed.\n\n  sherpa-onnx, DEFAULT arm -- 28 situations / 47 collapsed pairs, count\n  unchanged in both arms:\n        analysis_method   before {ddg_mixed 18, structural 6, ddg 4}\n                          after  {ddg_mixed 19, structural 4, ddg 5}\n        walk_verdict      before {not_attempted 13, unavailable 6, confirmed 4, escaped 5}\n                          after  {not_attempted 13, unavailable 4, confirmed 5, escaped 6}\n        method-rooted findings: 3 of 28 -- which is WHY the movement is small.\n\n  podman-compose, DEFAULT arm -- the qualitative result is the interesting one.\n  ONE structural finding with collapsed_flow_count=2 became TWO separately\n  verdicted situations:\n        before  _parse_args -> print_help   structural / unavailable  (2 pairs fused)\n        after   _parse_args -> basicConfig  ddg        / CONFIRMED\n                _parse_args -> print_help   ddg_mixed  / escaped\n  The fix DISTINGUISHES where it previously FUSED, and the confirmed one is the\n  flow that really carries argv into a log sink.\n\n  podman-compose, --include-non-production-sources -- the total case, and it\n  confirms WI-mojaz's premise outright:\n        100% of findings are METHOD-ROOTED (7 before, 8 after)\n        analysis_method   before {structural 7}   after {ddg_mixed 7, ddg 1}\n        walk_verdict      before {unavailable 7}  after {not_attempted 6, escaped 1, confirmed 1}\n  structural 7 -> 0. Every finding on that arm moves to a walk-backed label.\n\nVERDICT: no measured precision regression, and no mechanism for one by the route\nI feared. The distribution moves toward walk-backed labels, one collapsed blob\nresolves into a confirmed and an escaped finding, and the finding count moves\n+1 (a split), not down.\n\nTHE REAL RESIDUAL IS LABEL HONESTY, AND IT IS A DIFFERENT QUESTION.\ntaint.py::method_for_walk_verdict maps confirmed -> ddg, unavailable ->\nstructural, and EVERYTHING ELSE -- including not_attempted -- to ddg_mixed. Its\ndocstring says this is deliberate (\"three verdicts share ddg_mixed, which is\nprecisely the collapse INV-zidur exists to make visible\"). The consequence is\nnow measured: on the non-production arm 6 of 8 findings carry a DDG label with\nNO WALK EVER ATTEMPTED, gaining it from DDG COVERAGE rather than from evidence.\nWhether a not_attempted finding should read as ddg_mixed is an owner question\nabout a published vocabulary, so it is surfaced here, not decided.\n\nSTILL NOT DONE, and it needs a human: an actual useful-precision NUMBER. That\nrequires per-flow TP/FP adjudication against the ADR-0001 rubric via\nmeasure-taint-precision.py's collect/sample/score/packet cycle. The population\nabove is the input that cycle never had. WI-mojaz's ~76% FP figure for the\nnon-production arm is the obvious thing to re-derive on it."  # df75
